WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.314
Welcome to OurWater.

00:00:02.434 --> 00:00:09.250
After this video you can find any station in your
list, narrow it down, put it in order, and open it.

00:00:10.083 --> 00:00:14.307
Every well, rain gauge or pond you look after
is a station.

00:00:14.427 --> 00:00:18.243
To see yours together, click My stations in
the menu.

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:20.922
This is your list.

00:00:21.042 --> 00:00:25.290
Under the title, OurWater says how many
stations you can see.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.642
Here, twenty-four.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.322
Two tiles sum it up.

00:00:30.442 --> 00:00:33.466
Assigned stations is how many you look after.

00:00:33.586 --> 00:00:36.490
Last updated shows the newest measurement.

00:00:37.317 --> 00:00:42.189
Beside the search box is Add a station, for
registering a new water point.

00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:46.281
To find a station fast, type in Search.

00:00:46.401 --> 00:00:52.497
Use part of a name, a code, a village, a
country, a kind, or a note.

00:00:53.317 --> 00:00:57.349
The list shrinks as you type, and matching
letters light up.

00:00:57.469 --> 00:00:59.341
Nothing to press.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:02.454
A kind of station works too.

00:01:02.574 --> 00:01:05.526
Typing rain finds every rain gauge.

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:09.566
If nothing matches, you see this message.

00:01:09.686 --> 00:01:12.470
Check your spelling, or clear the box.

00:01:13.283 --> 00:01:16.091
Clear the box and the whole list returns.

00:01:16.917 --> 00:01:22.173
Next, click Show filters to open the tools for
narrowing and arranging your list.

00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:25.791
First, the station type chips.

00:01:25.911 --> 00:01:29.103
One for each kind you have, with how many.

00:01:29.223 --> 00:01:31.575
All is chosen to begin with.

00:01:32.383 --> 00:01:36.511
Click a chip, like Rainfall, to see only that
kind.

00:01:36.631 --> 00:01:38.791
Now just the rain gauges.

00:01:39.617 --> 00:01:41.945
Click All for everything again.

00:01:42.065 --> 00:01:47.009
Kinds you have none of are tucked away; Show
all brings them back, greyed out.

00:01:47.817 --> 00:01:49.905
Display chooses the look.

00:01:50.025 --> 00:01:51.897
List is a table.

00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:54.777
Grid shows each station as a card.

00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:59.951
Station status can show All, or only Active
stations.

00:02:00.071 --> 00:02:03.647
Mine are all active, so nothing changes.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.234
Group by puts stations under headings.

00:02:07.354 --> 00:02:11.002
Choose Station type, and each kind gets a
heading.

00:02:11.817 --> 00:02:15.825
Or group by village or town, to keep each
place together.

00:02:16.650 --> 00:02:19.146
Hide filters tidies the page.

00:02:19.266 --> 00:02:22.818
The small number reminds you that filters are
still working.

00:02:23.650 --> 00:02:25.522
Now the table.

00:02:25.642 --> 00:02:33.802
Each row is a station: name and code, village,
country, date added, last measurement, and kind.

00:02:34.617 --> 00:02:37.377
Beside each name is a small label.

00:02:37.497 --> 00:02:40.161
My station means you registered it.

00:02:40.281 --> 00:02:44.097
Others may say Shared, Team or Organisation.

00:02:44.917 --> 00:02:48.877
The list starts in order of station name, A to
Z.

00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:51.781
The small arrow shows the sorting column.

00:02:52.583 --> 00:02:55.103
Click a heading again to flip the order.

00:02:55.223 --> 00:02:57.095
Now Z to A.

00:02:57.917 --> 00:03:00.653
Village or Town sorts by place.

00:03:01.483 --> 00:03:03.715
Country sorts by country.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.229
Date added puts the oldest first.

00:03:07.349 --> 00:03:09.365
Click again for the newest.

00:03:10.183 --> 00:03:13.711
Click Last measurement twice for the most
recent first.

00:03:13.831 --> 00:03:16.783
Stations with none yet drop to the bottom.

00:03:17.617 --> 00:03:20.617
Station type groups stations by kind.

00:03:21.417 --> 00:03:24.417
At the right of each row are two small
buttons.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.769
The plus starts a measurement.

00:03:26.889 --> 00:03:29.073
The map icon shows the map.

00:03:29.883 --> 00:03:34.155
The plus opens the measurement form with that
station already chosen.

00:03:34.983 --> 00:03:38.919
The map icon opens the map, centred on that
station.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:45.630
Back on the list, this line says which rows
you see: one to twenty, of twenty-four.

00:03:46.450 --> 00:03:51.514
Rows per page can be fifty, a hundred, two
hundred, or All.

00:03:51.634 --> 00:03:56.146
With fifty, all twenty-four fit, and the page
buttons go away.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:01.390
With twenty rows, Next and Prev move between
pages.

00:04:01.510 --> 00:04:04.630
This is page two, with the last four.

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:08.930
Click any row to open that station in a
pop-up.

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:14.402
At the top: its name, label, kind, code and
village.

00:04:15.217 --> 00:04:22.105
Below: the code, village, type of well, depth,
position, and last measurement.

00:04:22.917 --> 00:04:25.701
Add a measurement records something new here.

00:04:26.517 --> 00:04:29.709
View history lists every measurement made
here.

00:04:30.517 --> 00:04:33.541
Show on map finds the station on the map.

00:04:34.350 --> 00:04:37.566
Edit station lets you fix a name or a village.

00:04:38.383 --> 00:04:42.919
Open full page shows everything, with its
photo and QR code.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:49.990
Give to my organisation or Transfer hands the
station on to your organisation, another person,

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.982
or a group.

00:04:52.783 --> 00:04:55.567
Add to favourites keeps a station close.

00:04:55.687 --> 00:04:57.991
The button then says Favourited.

00:04:58.111 --> 00:05:00.655
Find favourites in the Account menu.

00:05:01.483 --> 00:05:05.875
Close the pop-up with the X, a click outside
it, or Escape.

00:05:06.683 --> 00:05:08.915
That is your list of stations.

00:05:09.035 --> 00:05:11.699
Thanks for helping look after our water.
